  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given equation of ellipse is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>36</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>It is of the form&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>With&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>.</p><p>The centre of the circle is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be the common point for ellipse and circle.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Equation of normal to the ellipse will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>&#952;</mi></mstyle></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>sec&#952;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mi>cosec&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p><p>But the normal through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;passes through the centre of the circle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>6</mn><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mi>sec&#952;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mi>cosec&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>sec&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>27</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>65</mn></msqrt><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>65</mn></msqrt><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>65</mn></msqrt><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>65</mn></msqrt><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>69</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>69</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>92</mn></math></p><p>Therefore, the required answer is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>92</mn></math></p>",
